Alex scoffed. “Oh yeah? And why’s that?”

Make them believe you. Sell it, you don’t have another choice. I reminded myself.

“You just think I don’t belong here,” I said instead, something desperate lacing my words. My breath was uneven, my hands clenching into the fabric of my pajama pants. “You think I’m temporary—you’ve always thought that—but Liam…” My voice cracked. “He doesn’t.”

