Alex’s expression didn’t change. But something in her eyes did.

Chloe slid closer, her fingers wrapping gently around my wrist, squeezing lightly. “Caroline,” she murmured, voice soft. “You do belong here.”

A lump rose in my throat.

I looked at Alex. She held my stare for a long moment, something unreadable passing over her features.

Then she sighed, rubbing her temples like this was giving her a headache. “I just don’t want to watch you get swallowed whole.”
