She let me. She let me, but she wasn’t with me. Not the way she was with them. I’d watched

her with Chloe and Alex, seen the way she lit up, the way she laughed. That laugh—the kind that came without hesitation, without restraint—was something she never gave me.

Why couldn’t she be happy with me?
