I smirked.

We moved toward the shopping district just off campus, where polished storefronts lined the streets, their windows gleaming with carefully curated displays.

Caroline’s steps slowed when she realized. I didn’t let her stop. My grip on her hand tightened just enough to remind her—to warn her—before I pulled her forward. She stiffened, but she followed. She always would.

